The root cause of the compilation errors is a syntax error in `tests/kernel/queue/src/main.c`. The function `queue_test_setup` is missing its closing brace `}`. This causes the subsequent `ZTEST_SUITE` macro invocations to be parsed as if they were inside the function body.

`ZTEST_SUITE` is intended for file-scope usage. When used inside a function, it defines a non-static local struct (`ztest_suite_stats`) and then attempts to use its address to initialize a `static const` struct. The address of a non-static local variable is not a constant expression, leading to the `initializer element is not constant` error. The compiler gets confused by this and reports the error in the included header file `zephyr/ztest_test.h` on an unrelated line.

Fixing the syntax error by adding the closing brace for `queue_test_setup` will place the `ZTEST_SUITE` calls at the correct file scope, resolving the compilation errors. The Kconfig warning is likely a side-effect of the build failing early and will be resolved once the compilation succeeds.

